\f2\i  Dawkins, you can swap Dawkins out for anything.
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dr Carpenter lifted his head, and for the first time his voice sounded less like a sermon and more like a man trying to speak in his own mouth. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Praise\'85\'94 he began again, and stopped, as if startled by himself. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kathy forced air into her lungs. \'93Don\'92t,\'94 she said. \'93One repetition. That\'92s enough.\'94 She didn\'92t need to be around for the full entrainment. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleo finally looked at her. His expression held no comfort at all.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis grunted, satisfied. \'93We can deploy this,\'94 he said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Praise the Dawkins.\'94 Dr Carpenter smiled.
